---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import FAQList from '../components/FAQList.astro';
import PlanningCTA from '../components/PlanningCTA.astro';
import { images } from '../data/assets';
import { culturalPages } from '../data/landing';
const breadcrumbs=[{label:'Cultural & Cruise Travel',href:'/cultural-cruise-travel/'}];
const formats=[
  {title:'Hosted Cultural Journeys',copy:'Food, history, neighborhoods, local context, and shared discovery with enough time for travelers to experience the destination rather than race through it.',image:images.marrakech,tags:['Culture','Hosted','Private groups'],href:'/cultural-cruise-travel/cultural-group-travel/'},
  {title:'Hosted Cruise Groups',copy:'Use a cruise as the travel backbone while coordinating arrivals, cabin choices, shared experiences, pre- and post-cruise stays, and group communication.',image:images.boat,tags:['Cruise','Coastal','Social'],href:'/cultural-cruise-travel/hosted-cruises/'},
  {title:'City & Region Discovery',copy:'Curated urban and regional travel that balances guided experiences, local food, independent time, and realistic group movement.',image:images.culture,tags:['Cities','Discovery','Flexible'],href:'/plan-a-trip/'},
  {title:'Active Cultural Travel',copy:'Walk, hike, paddle, cycle, or move through a region while keeping culture and place at the center of the itinerary.',image:images.paddle,tags:['Active rest','Culture','Movement'],href:'/trekking-active-travel/'}
];
const faqs=[
  {q:'What is cultural group travel?',a:'Cultural group travel is an itinerary built around shared discovery of a destination through local history, food, neighborhoods, landscapes, events, people, and selected activities. A private cultural trip can include guided experiences and organized logistics while still leaving meaningful independent time.'},
  {q:'How does a hosted cruise group differ from booking the same sailing independently?',a:'A hosted group adds a group-planning layer around the cruise. That can include cabin and booking coordination, common arrival plans, transfers, pre- or post-cruise stays, selected group meals or excursions, organizer communication, and a clearer shared program.'},
  {q:'Do cultural trips have to be low activity?',a:'No. Cultural travel can include substantial walking, hiking, cycling, paddling, food tours, or other active experiences. The itinerary should describe the physical demand clearly and match it to the group.'},
  {q:'Can travelers have free time on a private group trip?',a:'Yes. Free time is often essential. A well-designed itinerary protects important shared experiences while leaving room for rest, independent meals, shopping, museums, local exploration, or simply time away from the group.'},
  {q:'Can a cultural trip be built for older active travelers?',a:'Yes. The planning should focus on mobility, pace, comfort, activity tolerance, rooming, transfers, and the actual traveler profile rather than using age as a substitute for those details.'}
];
const serviceSchema={'@type':'Service',name:'Cultural and Cruise Group Travel',description:'Private cultural group travel and hosted cruise planning with itinerary design, group coordination, pre- and post-travel, local experiences, and organizer support.',provider:{'@id':`${Astro.site}#organization`},areaServed:{'@type':'Place',name':'Worldwide'}};
const faqSchema={'@type':'FAQPage',mainEntity:faqs.map(i=>({'@type':'Question',name:i.q,acceptedAnswer:{'@type':'Answer',text:i.a}}))};
---
<BaseLayout title="Cultural & Cruise Group Travel | Talon Expeditions" description="Private cultural group travel and hosted cruise planning for clubs, communities, social groups, businesses, and private travelers, with worldwide coordination and flexible pacing." image={images.culture} breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs} schema={[serviceSchema,faqSchema]}>
  <section class="page-hero" style={`background-image:url('${images.culture}')`}><div class="shell"><Breadcrumbs items={breadcrumbs}/><p class="eyebrow">Culture & Cruise</p><h1 class="section-title">Shared journeys with time to discover, connect, and actually enjoy being there.</h1><p>Culture-led itineraries, hosted cruise groups, scenic travel, and comfort-forward journeys for people who want useful structure without turning the trip into a schedule they have to survive.</p></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell definition-grid"><div class="definition-sticky"><p class="eyebrow">Direct answer</p><h2>What does Talon mean by cultural and hosted group travel?</h2></div><div class="definition-body"><div class="answer-panel"><p>Cultural and hosted group travel combines coordinated logistics with selected shared experiences, local context, and enough flexibility for travelers to enjoy the destination at their own pace. The format can include private cultural itineraries, cruise groups, coastal journeys, city-and-region travel, food and heritage programs, or lighter active experiences.</p></div><h2>Experience-led does not have to mean high-intensity.</h2><p>Some groups want a summit or a skill progression. Others want to travel with people they know, understand a place more deeply, eat well, move enough to feel engaged, and return to comfortable accommodation at the end of the day. That is still experience-led travel.</p><p>The planning work is often about rhythm. A cultural itinerary can look excellent on paper and still be exhausting if every transfer, meal, tour, museum, and evening is scheduled. A hosted cruise can feel easy operationally but disconnected socially if nobody defines when the group actually comes together. Talon helps shape those details around the people traveling.</p></div></div></section>

  <section class="specialty-intro soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Ways to travel</p><h2 class="section-title">Choose the rhythm before filling the calendar.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">Different groups want different balances of guided time, independent exploration, comfort, activity, social time, and movement between destinations.</p></div><div class="destination-grid">{formats.map(item=><a class="destination-card" href={item.href} style={`background-image:url('${item.image}')`}><div class="destination-content"><span class="tagline">Group format</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.copy}</p><div class="mini-tags">{item.tags.map(tag=><span>{tag}</span>)}</div></div></a>)}</div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell split-copy-image"><div><p class="eyebrow">The pacing matters</p><h2 class="section-title">Enough structure to make the trip rich. Enough space to make it feel like travel.</h2><p class="section-copy">For most cultural groups, the strongest itinerary has a few anchor experiences each day rather than a continuous chain of appointments. Travel time, meals, walking, hotel changes, jet lag, and the simple fact that groups move more slowly than individuals all need to be included honestly.</p><p class="section-copy">Free time is also part of the design. Travelers should know what is nearby, when they need to rejoin the group, and which optional activities require advance planning. That gives people independence without making the itinerary feel unsupported.</p><div class="chip-row"><span class="chip">Culture & heritage</span><span class="chip">Food & local life</span><span class="chip">Cruise & coast</span><span class="chip">Light activity</span><span class="chip">Hosted social travel</span><span class="chip">Comfort-forward pacing</span></div><a class="button" href="/cultural-cruise-travel/cultural-group-travel/">Explore Cultural Group Travel</a></div><div class="split-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.city}')`}></div></div></section>

  <section class="section tabbed-feature"><div class="shell tabbed-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Choose your rhythm</p><h2 class="section-title">Not every day needs the same energy.</h2><ul class="category-menu"><li class="active">Guided discovery</li><li>Independent time</li><li>Hosted meals & social time</li><li>Light active experiences</li><li>Scenic travel days</li><li>Rest without guilt</li></ul></div><div class="category-feature" style={`background-image:url('${images.paddle}')`}><div class="feature-note"><h3>A trip can be active and comfortable at the same time.</h3><p>The goal is a journey that gives people reasons to engage without asking every traveler to perform at the same level every day.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell process-donor"><div class="process-visual" style={`background-image:url('${images.marrakech}')`}><div class="process-callout"><h3>Anchor the journey.</h3><p>Choose the experiences worth organizing around, then let the itinerary breathe between them.</p></div></div><div><p class="eyebrow">How we shape it</p><h2 class="section-title">Build from the shared interest outward.</h2><p class="section-copy">A cultural or hosted trip is easier to design when the organizer can explain what the group wants from the experience beyond “see as much as possible.” The purpose becomes the filter for every itinerary choice.</p><div class="process-list"><div class="process-item"><b>Define the group</b><p>Who is traveling together, what connects them, and what pace or comfort expectations matter?</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Choose anchor experiences</b><p>Identify the culture, cruise, food, history, event, region, or shared interest that makes the trip worth taking.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Set the pace</b><p>Balance guided time, movement, social time, independent exploration, meals, and recovery.</p></div><div class="process-item"><b>Coordinate the practical pieces</b><p>Connect lodging, transport, reservations, operators, tickets, arrivals, rooming, and traveler information.</p></div></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section dark-section"><div class="shell mission-grid"><div><p class="eyebrow">Hosted cruise groups</p><h2 class="section-title">The ship can handle the route. The group still needs a plan.</h2><p style="color:#aaa">Travelers may choose different cabins, arrive from different cities, want different excursions, or add extra nights. A hosted group layer can make those choices easier to coordinate without requiring everybody to follow the same schedule onboard.</p><a class="button" href="/cultural-cruise-travel/hosted-cruises/">How Hosted Cruise Groups Work</a></div><div class="mission-stack"><div class="mission-card"><h3>Before the cruise</h3><p>Cabin and booking structure, arrival timing, hotel nights, transfers, documents, and a clear embarkation plan.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>During the cruise</h3><p>Selected shared meals or experiences, optional shore time, group communication, and enough independence to enjoy the ship.</p></div><div class="mission-card"><h3>After the cruise</h3><p>Disembarkation, transfers, onward flights, extra nights, or a cultural extension that adds depth beyond the sailing.</p></div></div></div></section>

  <section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Cultural & hosted travel paths</p><h2 class="section-title">Go deeper into the format that fits the group.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">These pages explain the planning differences between cruise groups and land-based cultural travel rather than treating them as interchangeable products.</p></div><div class="category-card-grid">{culturalPages.map(page=><a class="category-card" href={`/cultural-cruise-travel/${page.slug}/`}><div class="category-card-image" style={`background-image:url('${page.hero}')`}></div><div class="category-card-body"><h3>{page.title}</h3><p>{page.description}</p><span>Explore this trip type →</span></div></a>)}<a class="category-card" href="/group-travel/social-affinity/"><div class="category-card-image" style={`background-image:url('${images.group}')`}></div><div class="category-card-body"><h3>Travel for Social & Affinity Groups</h3><p>Hosted travel for communities whose members already share an interest, identity, organization, or reason to spend time together.</p><span>See the group planning model →</span></div></a></div></div></section>

  <section class="section soft-section"><div class="shell"><div class="specialty-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Common questions</p><h2 class="section-title">What organizers ask before choosing a cultural or cruise format.</h2></div><p class="section-copy">The specific cruise line, destination, supplier, and written trip terms determine the final booking conditions.</p></div><FAQList items={faqs} openFirst={true}/></div></section>

  <PlanningCTA title="Want a group trip that feels organized without feeling over-programmed?" copy="Start with the people and the kind of shared experience you want. We can help choose whether a cultural land itinerary, hosted cruise, active-rest format, or hybrid structure makes the most sense." />
</BaseLayout>
